Thebooleankeyword is a data type that can only take the valuestrueorfalse.

Boolean values are mostly used for conditional testing (read theJava Booleans Tutorialfor more information).

Read more about data types in ourJava Data Types Tutorial.

Read more about booleans in ourJava Booleans Tutorial.

❮ Java Keywords

### Code Examples

```
Example
A boolean data type with true or false values:
boolean isJavaFun = true;
boolean isFishTasty = false;
System.out.println(isJavaFun);     // Outputs true
System.out.println(isFishTasty);   // Outputs false
Try it Yourself »
```

## Tutorials

❮ Java Keywords

Thebreakkeyword is used to break out aforloop, awhileloop or aswitchblock.

Use thecontinuekeyword to end the current iteration in a loop, but continue with the next.

Read more about for loops in ourJava For Loops Tutorial.

Read more about while loops in ourJava While Loops Tutorial.

Read more about break and continue in ourJava Break Tutorial.

❮ Java Keywords

### Code Examples

```
Example
End the loop when
i
is equal to 4:
for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
  if (i == 4) {
    break;
  }
  System.out.println(i);
}
Try it Yourself »

---

Example
Break out of a while loop:
int i = 0;
while (i < 10) {
  System.out.println(i);
  i++;
  if (i == 4) {
    break;
  }
}
Try it Yourself »
```

